    {
      "bbox": [
        432,
        1212,
        1221,
        1418
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "No liability is to be contracted for in excess of funds available for the purpose. The head of a department or other agency shall be held strictly accountable for exceeding appropriations without specific itemized approval of the Mayor. All balances of appropriations for which no contract liability is registered on the books of the Office of the Comptroller shall expire six months after the close of the 1977 fiscal year and disposed of pursuant to law, except for encumbered balances in General Purchase Fund accounts, which shall expire one year after the close of the 1977 fiscal year. The Department of Purchase shall accept no requisitions encumbering appropriations after June 30, 1977, and for purposes of efficient operation may set an earlier date. Agencies shall place neither orders chargeable to, nor further encumbrances on, annual requirement contracts issued for the fiscal year 1977 after June 30, 1977.",
